      "There is a safety dimension too. Deep water on a solid cover looks solid but is not, and children or pets may be tempted to step on it. Keep the cover fenced or otherwise inaccessible, and never treat it as a walking surface. A cover that is properly drained and taut is safer and performs better, and it lasts longer because it is not carrying unnecessary load through freeze-thaw cycles.",
      "Water on a solid cover is normal, but standing water is a maintenance signal. Address the drainage, keep the panel and pump working, and avoid adding weight. With a little attention, the cover will shed water, protect the pool, and open clean in spring. If the problem recurs despite your efforts, have the cover inspected for sagging, stretched straps, or a poorly placed panel before the next winter.",
